  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA-only models outperform image-only resnet50, that multiprofile avgpool improves PCA RNA from 0.485 to 0.591, and that scvi_n200 with multiprofile avgpool reaches the best result at 0.650 accuracy and 0.628 F1. The key uncertainty is whether scvi_n200 is intrinsically a better representation or whether its gain mainly comes from multiprofile aggregation. config_004 tests scvi_n200 in the singleprofile setting, changing only the RNA encoder relative to config_001. This cleanly isolates the representation effect, clarifies whether a simpler singleprofile scvi model can approach the best result, and avoids changing multiple design choices at once, making it a high-information next experiment under a limited budget."
}

